.5},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 1 daily record high, no daily record lows","records":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","change":"Spokane's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days show no clear change.","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 50\u00b0F was the 22nd warmest November 13 high (tied) of 146 since 1881, the warmest since 2025.","t_yest":"November 13: warmer than 83% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>50\u00b0F</strong> was the 22nd warmest November 13 high (tied) of 146 since 1881, the warmest since 2025. The normal high for the date is 44\u00b0F, and the record is 60\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>40\u00b0F</strong> was the 9th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 146 since 1881.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Spokane's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Spokane has set <strong>39 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 67 that chance alone would give, and <strong>74 record highs</strong>, close to the 67 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (52). Spokane's all-time high is 109\u00b0F, on June 29, 2021.","t_chg":"Spokane's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days show no clear change.","p_chg":"Across 144 complete years: Spokane's average low shows no clear change: +0.02\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.04 to +0.09) that includes zero. Spokane's average high shows no clear change: \u22120.04\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.10 to +0.03) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+1.06\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.71 to +1.41) and highs show no clear change. The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months; 3 months fell. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months; 3 months fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Spokane's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.01 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 16.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1948 (26.07 in); the driest, 1929 (7.54 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 1 daily record high, no daily record lows"}}